	doi = {10.1007/978-1-4615-0429-0_11},
	abstract = {Software design patterns describe simple and elegant solutions to specific design problems. Design patterns capture design knowledge that have been discovered, evolved over time and proven to be effective in solving design problems. Application of design patterns improves software productivity and quality. Therefore the use of design patterns is rapidly increasing. However, it is not an easy task to choose an appropriate pattern to be applied from among the plethora of patterns. This is partly due to the learning curve involved to understand what each pattern can do for the designer. In this paper we present a methodology for constructing expert systems which can suggest design patterns to solve a designer's design problems. The methodology details the knowledge acquisition, knowledge representation and expert systems implementation activities. It is illustrated through the prototyping of the Expert System for Suggesting Design Patterns ({ESSDP}). Evaluation of the {ESSDP} by subjects other than the original developers indicates that the system indeed could suggest the needed design patterns effectively.},
